{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"CI run 32620281081 failed three deterministic contract tests on every matrix job. The same failures reproduced locally. F12 made intercept help discoverable, which exposed stale compatibility and output inventories that assumed those help arms were absent. ADR 0100 requires the `jira-onboard` compatibility shim to remain visible, and the approved F12 plan requires the overview omit set to remain unchanged. The schema guard permits explicit exemptions for operations that cannot run in CI. The plan and file impact now cover compatibility classification, schema registration, offline drivers, model-operation exemptions, schema comments, and the output catalog. A fresh normal plan review will run before file edits."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1787465098532756001,"uuid":"b2285505-747e-49f2-b38e-60d2809d37b5"}